cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying manuscript."
title: "RadFusion PE — independent reproduction, interpretability, and label-leakage audit"
authors:
  - family-names: Jaffar
    given-names: Zain A.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1273-3030"
    affiliation: "Rutgers University, New Brunswick, NJ, USA"
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  Code reproducing multimodal late-fusion pulmonary-embolism detection on the public Stanford AIMI
  RadFusion benchmark. The imaging arm reuses the benchmark's provided (PENet-derived) study-level
  vision-model scores; the EHR arm is re-implemented as an elastic-net logistic model (with a
  support-vector variant); the two are combined by average/maximum late fusion, and the EHR arm is
  audited with SHAP. The audit surfaces a temporal label-leakage risk in the benchmark.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >
    A Multimodal Late-Fusion Pipeline for Pulmonary Embolism Detection from CT Pulmonary Angiography
    and Electronic Health Records, with Interpretable EHR Feature Attribution: A Reproducibility Study
  authors:
    - family-names: Jaffar
